# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The steel profiles as linear types: IPE, IPN, HEA, HEB, HEM
# (EN 10365, DIN 1025), UPN, UPE (EN 10365, DIN 1026), equal and unequal
# angles (EN 10056-1), T sections (EN 10055), square, rectangular and
# circular hollow sections (EN 10210), and the further steel series of the
# catalogue (HEAA, HD, the historic DIE, DIL, DIN and DIR, UAP, cold-formed
# hollow sections and lipped C sections, flat and round bars), each with its
# IFC profile (`bim_profiles.dl`: an I, U, L, T, C shape, a hollow section,
# a rectangle, a circle; IPN's tapered flanges as parallel ones), named by
# its designation ("HEA 200", "L 80x80x8", "CHS 114.3x5", "HD 260x93"), of
# steel, with the NL-SfB code 28.1 (main load-bearing structure). Beams take
# every profile; the IPE and H sections and the hollow sections are columns
# too. The dimensions are the profile catalogue's
# (`elements/linear/profiles/*.json`, read through
# `bim_profile_catalogue.dl`): depth h, width b, web tw, flange tf and root
# radius r (an angle's thickness as tw and tf; a hollow section's wall as tw
# and its outer corner radius as tf). This adds the whole steel catalogue at
# once; the Profiles tab adds one profile when it is used (`add bim
# catalogue profile`).
import elements/linear/bim_profile_catalogue.dl

# The library loaded once: 1 at 2000100 of the project.
function bim steel library setting:
    replacement:
        2000100

# The steel profiles added to `target` as linear types, once (none when the
# library was loaded before), named by the rules once all are in. The ids
# made.
function add bim eu steel profiles to {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        set made to a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer
        if (the bim setting (bim steel library setting) of (0 as a 64 bit integer) in (@intrinsic("dereference", target)))'s found:
            return made
        # The steel series of the profile catalogue, appended directly; the
        # rules name them all at the end, but for a series whose profiles
        # keep their catalogue name (HD, Cw), given here.
        set seriesList to the bim profile catalogue series
        loop seriesCursor from 0 to the length of seriesList:
            set seriesValue to the item at seriesCursor in seriesList
            if bim catalogue series seriesValue's code is european steel:
                set seriesProfiles to the bim catalogue profiles of series (seriesValue's code)
                loop profileCursor from 0 to the length of seriesProfiles:
                    set catalogueProfile to the item at profileCursor in seriesProfiles
                    loop roleCursor from 0 to 2:
                        set roleCode to bim beam role
                        if roleCursor = 1:
                            set roleCode to bim column role
                        if (roleCursor = 0) or catalogueProfile's columnToo:
                            set fresh to append bim catalogue profile catalogueProfile as role roleCode to target
                            if fresh != the bim refused id:
                                append fresh to (made's values)
                                if seriesValue's keepsName:
                                    set bim property (the string form of "Name") of set (the string form of "Type identity") of fresh to catalogueProfile's name typed (the string form of "IFCLABEL") in target
                free seriesProfiles
        free seriesList
        set bim setting (bim steel library setting) of (0 as a 64 bit integer) to (1 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
        name bim types by the rules in target
        return made
